//
// Expected: u1 at one session and at two.
//
// b is a weak hash of a and y, so breaking b hands the attacker a and y, and
// the a inside b is the a on the wire. The attacker can rebuild b only from
// what it opened out of b, but every one of those leaves comes out of b
// alone, so comparing them with a is a real test: u1.
//
// A rebuild that ties one queried value to the other counts only when each of
// its leaves is still derivable after withholding one of the two values. That
// keeps this link and rejects the one in unlink_shares_recomposed_secret.vp,
// where share_b is rebuilt from share_a and the secret recomposed from both,
// which any two points satisfy (GitHub issue #51). Rejecting every rebuild
// that needs the rebuilt value itself would lose this link too.
attacker[passive]

principal Alice[
	generates a, y
	b = HASH[weak](a, y)
]

Alice -> Bob: a, b

principal Bob[
	_ = HASH(a, b)
]

queries[
	unlinkability? a, b
]
